0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 671.8112598425196893 Td
(In the standard hospital diagnostics lifecycle, patients arrive with physician test orders that require clinical billing clearance prior to) Tj
T* (sample procurement and laboratory testing. Previously, once an order was billed and the technician initiated specimen collection,) Tj
T* (the system redirected the user to a secondary Phlebotomy & Sample Collection queue. This created administrative friction,) Tj
T* (repetitive click-paths, and delayed diagnostic turnaround times \(TAT\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (As requested by hospital operations, the Phlebotomy module and intermediate sample collection queue have been completely) Tj
T* (removed. When a billed patient sample is drawn, the system now automatically synchronizes specimen collection state and) Tj
T* (directly dispatches the order into the Department Analytical Worklists \(Hematology, Clinical Biochemistry, Microbiology & Serology,) Tj
T* (Clinical Pathology & Urinalysis, or Histopathology & Cytology\) based on test type.) Tj
ET
